    "updated_at": "2026-11-11T12:11:33Z",
    "body": "For whoever picks this up after #781 (PR #831, merge-ready), notes from its review:\n- **Cost after a flip:** cutting a carried field after a flip is about 35-40x dearer than upright. One slot on a 40×30 block takes 83-148 ms in release (2.4 ms upright) and 1.1-1.8 s in debug. The bake itself takes microseconds; a half turn about Z with no flip costs the same as upright. Budget for this, or pin the cost, before moving the holders onto the field engine.\n- **Composing flips:** build composed turns with `CarriedField::then`, not by composing before `new()`, or the sticky `flipped` flag is lost (the unsafe direction for `floor_judged`). Also, `turn` is a pub field; a direct write would leave the flag stale. Consider making it read-only.",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
